WEBVTT

00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:02.913
allowed it to fly less than
five nanometers above the disc's surface,

00:03:02.913 --> 00:03:06.288
about the width of two strands of DNA.

00:03:06.663 --> 00:03:08.413
For the past several decades,

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.954
the exponential growth in computer
storage capacity and processing power

00:03:11.996 --> 00:03:15.704
has followed a pattern
known as “Moore’s Law”,

00:03:15.746 --> 00:03:19.454
which, in 1975,
predicted that information density

00:03:19.496 --> 00:03:21.996
would double every two years.

00:03:22.038 --> 00:03:25.954
But at around 100 gigabits
per square inch,

00:03:25.996 --> 00:03:29.288
shrinking the magnetic grains further
or cramming them closer together

00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:34.288
posed a new risk called 
“the superparamagnetic effect”.